From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] autoconf 2.72+ compat: add AC_INIT reference for detection

autoconf 2.72+ autoreconf uses a word-boundary regex /\bAC_INIT\b/ to
verify that configure.ac is an autoconf script before proceeding.

The scan strips dnl comments and shell # comments before applying the
regex, so a dnl comment containing AC_INIT does not work. The scan
looks for AC_INIT as a literal word (not inside another macro name).

krb5 calls AC_INIT indirectly via K5_AC_INIT (defined in aclocal.m4).
The K5_ prefix prevents the word-boundary match since _ is a word char.

Add an m4_ifndef guard as a no-op stub whose argument contains AC_INIT
as a standalone word. Since AC_INIT is always defined when autoconf
processes this file, m4_ifndef never fires; it is purely a detection
hint for autoreconf's scanner.
---
 src/configure.ac | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/configure.ac b/src/configure.ac
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/src/configure.ac
+++ b/src/configure.ac
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
+dnl autoconf 2.72+ strips dnl/# comments then checks /\bAC_INIT\b/.
+dnl K5_AC_INIT (below) calls AC_INIT but the K5_ prefix breaks word boundary.
+m4_ifndef([AC_INIT], [m4_fatal([AC_INIT not available])])
 K5_AC_INIT([aclocal.m4])

 # If $runstatedir isn't set by autoconf (<2.70), set it manually.
